  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d6865b1-5599-46f0-b257-8dace8b74e45"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives a list of ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " vertex sets of the class named by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Properties"]], "paclet:ref/Properties"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "211f2bd2-2c0b-4946-a78f-56039f6fe172"],
 "."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"c382d839-c7ee-43f6-85cf-c745eb77f61a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bisector is ",
 StyleBox["H(p\:2081, p\:2082) = {v : d(p\:2081, v) = d(p\:2082, v)}", "TI"],
 ". In the plane it is the perpendicular bisector, a line; here it is a \
vertex set."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"725b9aec-d11f-405a-ac81-c3917d603957"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On a bipartite graph, such as the square grid, ",
 StyleBox["d(p\:2081, v) \[Minus] d(p\:2082, v)", "TI"],
 " has the parity of ",
 StyleBox["d(p\:2081, p\:2082)", "TI"],
 ". So the bisector is empty when ",
 StyleBox["d(p\:2081, p\:2082)", "TI"],
 " is odd, and the slab {\[Minus]1, 1} is then the vertices at difference \
\[PlusMinus]1. On the mesh the bisector at odd distance is usually not \
empty."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"26d451f3-763b-4c47-b2a3-75348c971a8b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bisector need not separate ",
 StyleBox["p\:2081", "TI"],
 " from ",
 StyleBox["p\:2082", "TI"],
 ". On the grid it does; on the mesh a path can step across it from a vertex \
nearer ",
 StyleBox["p\:2081", "TI"],
 " to a vertex nearer ",
 StyleBox["p\:2082", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a7b9574a-f57f-4a87-bcc6-f5c10ca753b8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The count ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " can be ",
 Cell[BoxData["n"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d81e50b-9c04-448d-9d35-1d4eaaeb6d80"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"UpTo", "[", "n", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b7521849-a686-43f9-b151-111011cd6028"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9bf952ea-2d33-4538-a841-8817bd74128e"],
 ". With the default ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Properties", " ", "->", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03654943-37ab-4fc9-b990-3213b1ea452a"],
 " the class has one set, the bisector or the slab itself."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"86713494-b8e5-413e-919e-5aa7d349218a"],

